    "done_when": "A review dispatch is exempt from the per-session queued-run cap enforced in reckon/crew/runs.py (where QueueFull is raised), and among one session's queued runs admission_order in reckon/crew/queue_order.py launches a review before an implementation node queued earlier; the cap still bounds every other role. New tests in tests/test_a_review_passes_its_sessions_queue_cap.py pass: a fixture session holding its cap of queued implementation nodes dispatches a review and gets it queued, not QueueFull; with one slot free, admission_order puts that review ahead of the earlier implementation nodes of the same session; a further implementation dispatch is still refused QueueFull, which is the control. The gate log shows the first two cases failing on the base commit. tests/test_queue_order.py is held by another run and is not edited; it is in the gate, and if the ordering change breaks one of its cases the manifest names the case and stops as blocked rather than changing it. Gate, run in place on the fleet allocation with its log under the run directory: PYTHONPATH=$PWD /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/reckon/.venv/bin/python -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider -q tests/test_a_review_passes_its_sessions_queue_cap.py tests/test_queue_order.py tests/test_a_queued_dispatch_is_accepted.py tests/test_a_queued_pointer_without_its_time_reads_no_place.py tests/test_queued_work_shows_where_held_work_shows.py tests/test_the_admission_pass_survives_a_pointer_without_its_time.py tests/test_a_queued_review_reports_queued.py tests/test_a_queued_run_is_admitted.py tests/test_every_module_fits_a_worker_window.py, judged by failure delta against the base revision; ruff check and ruff format --check clean on the changed paths. ",
